@startuml CycleFar Feedback Proposal Sequence
title CycleFar — Propose and apply a feedback adaptation

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "Owner-scoped\nRails controllers" as Controller
control "HorizonMaterializer" as Materializer
control "CompletionRecorder" as Recorder
control "FeedbackEvaluator" as Evaluator
control "ProposalComparison" as Comparison
control "FeedbackLoadLimiter" as Limiter
control "ProposalApplier" as Applier
control "ManualEditor" as Editor
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

== Complete workout and decide whether to propose ==
Rider -> Controller: POST completion with RPE and quality
Controller -> Recorder: call(owned structured workout)
group completion transaction
  Recorder -> Database: save feedback and immutable FTP/watt snapshot
  Recorder -> Evaluator: evaluate feedback
  Evaluator -> Database: read comparable planned workouts in today..day 13
  Evaluator -> Comparison: preview candidate changes
  Comparison -> Limiter: fit proposals against fixed load and ceilings
  Limiter -> Editor: preview canonical workout changes
  Editor --> Limiter: definitions and current-FTP metrics
  Limiter --> Comparison: bounded proposed prescriptions
  Comparison --> Evaluator: current/proposed metrics and bias
  opt meaningful change remains
    Evaluator --> Recorder: reason and proposal payload
    Recorder -> Database: save AdaptationProposal
  end
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar

== Review: proposal comparison does not change workouts ==
Rider -> Controller: GET calendar
Controller -> Materializer: materialize eligible near-term outlines
Materializer -> Database: save any newly due structured details
Controller -> Database: load this rider's pending proposals
Controller -> Comparison: calculate Current / Proposed values
alt proposal remains available
  Comparison -> Limiter: recheck target set and weekly load
  Limiter --> Comparison: in-memory fitted prescriptions
  Comparison --> Controller: before/after workouts and clamped bias
  Controller --> Rider: show comparison and Accept / Reject
else stale or invalid targets
  Comparison --> Controller: unavailable
  Controller --> Rider: show Reject only
end

== Decision ==
alt Reject (available or unavailable)
  Rider -> Controller: DELETE proposal
  Controller -> Database: load rider-owned proposal
  Controller -> Applier: reject!
  Applier -> Database: destroy proposal
else Accept (available proposal)
  Rider -> Controller: POST accept proposal
  Controller -> Database: load rider-owned proposal
  Controller -> Applier: accept!
  group transaction: lock plan, then proposal
    Applier -> Database: lock owned plan and proposal
    Applier -> Comparison: revalidate and recalculate whole target set
    Comparison -> Limiter: recheck current limits
    Limiter --> Comparison: fitted prescriptions
    Comparison --> Applier: accepted comparison
    loop each affected workout
      Applier -> Editor: apply! accepted definition
      Editor -> Database: replace planned steps and metrics
    end
    Applier -> Database: save clamped global bias; destroy proposal
  end
end
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar

note over Comparison, Database
  An unavailable comparison shows Reject only. The completed source
  remains immutable. Expiry is stored but is not currently enforced.
end note
@enduml
